    "content": "<div style='display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem'><span class='tag'>US Department of Health</span> <span class='tag'>1996</span></div>\n<h1>Energy / Utilities AI Compliance: HIPAA</h1>\n<p class='lead'>Utilities operating health-related programmes — wellness incentives, home-health monitoring partnerships, or medical-device power services — may process protected health information. When acting as business associates or handling PHI, HIPAA obligations apply.</p>\n\n<div class='meta-bar'>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>Sector:</strong> Energy / Utilities</span>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>Regulation:</strong> HIPAA</span>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>CSOAI Articles:</strong> 4 mapped</span>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Key Compliance Requirements</h2>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Business Associate Agreements for health-utility AI</h3><p>Utilities partnering with healthcare providers for remote monitoring or wellness programmes must sign BAAs and implement HIPAA safeguards.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Privacy Rule for health-utility AI</h3><p>AI systems processing health-related data from smart-home health devices or wellness programmes must respect the Minimum Necessary Standard.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Security Rule for health-utility systems</h3><p>Technical safeguards must protect electronic PHI in utility AI systems, with access controls and audit trails.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Breach Notification for health-utility data</h3><p>Unauthorised access to health-related data must be assessed under the Breach Notification Rule and reported where required.</p></div>\n\n<h2>CSOAI Charter Articles</h2>\n<ul class='articles'>\n<li>Article 25 — Privacy by Design</li>\n<li>Article 43 — Sovereignty Principle</li>\n<li>Article 47 — Audit Right</li>\n<li>Article 22 — Right to Safety</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Relevant MCPs</h2>\n<p style='color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem'>These MCP servers operationalise compliance for this sector and regulation:</p>\n<span class='mcp-tag'>hipaa-privacy-rule-checker-mcp</span> <span class='mcp-tag'>hipaa-security-rule-assessor-mcp</span> <span class='mcp-tag'>csoai-data-governance</span> \n\n<h2>Framework Reference</h2>\n<p>See the full <a href='/frameworks/hipaa'>HIPAA crosswalk</a> for the published clause-by-clause mappings. The signed crosswalk covers four regimes; anything outside them is described, not crosswalked.</p>\n\n<div class='cta'>\n  <h2>Run the free risk classifier</h2>\n  <p style='color:#e6f7ec;margin:.5rem 0'>The free self-serve tool is an EU AI Act risk classifier: describe the system in text and a deterministic decision table returns the Annex III tier and the gaps against a fixed Art 9–15/50 control set. It covers one regulation, it never contacts your system, and it is not a bench run. A GSPC bench run against a frozen bank is arranged directly and is not yet self-serve.</p>\n  <a href='/certify'>Get Measured &rarr;</a>\n  <a href='/asti'>See AI Self-State Index</a>\n  <a href='/frameworks'>All Frameworks</a>\n</div>\n\n<p class='foot'>&copy; 2026 CSOAI LTD &middot; UK Companies House <strong>16939677</strong><br>\nSector crosswalk &middot; CC BY 4.0 &middot; <a href='/methodology'>Methodology</a> &middot; <a href='mailto:nicholas@csoai.org'>Contact</a><br>\n<em>\"The ISO for AI safety.\"</em></p>",
