    "content": "<div style='display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem'><span class='tag'>European Union</span> <span class='tag'>2024</span></div>\n<h1>Finance / Banking AI Compliance: EU AI Act</h1>\n<p class='lead'>Credit scoring, fraud detection, and algorithmic trading systems are classified as high-risk under Annex III of the EU AI Act. Financial institutions must implement risk-management systems, ensure model accuracy, and maintain human oversight over consequential automated decisions.</p>\n\n<div class='meta-bar'>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>Sector:</strong> Finance / Banking</span>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>Regulation:</strong> EU AI Act</span>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>CSOAI Articles:</strong> 4 mapped</span>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Key Compliance Requirements</h2>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>High-risk classification for credit & fraud AI</h3><p>AI systems evaluating creditworthiness, detecting fraud, or making pricing decisions fall under Annex III high-risk and require full conformity assessments.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Accuracy, robustness & fairness metrics</h3><p>Article 15 requires documented accuracy targets, back-testing regimes, and fairness metrics to prevent discriminatory outcomes in lending and insurance pricing.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Human oversight for adverse decisions</h3><p>Article 14 mandates that humans with appropriate authority review AI-driven adverse credit decisions, with the ability to override or escalate.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Record-keeping & audit trails</h3><p>Article 12 requires automatic logging of AI system inputs, outputs, and human interventions to enable supervisory audits and post-incident reconstruction.</p></div>\n\n<h2>CSOAI Charter Articles</h2>\n<ul class='articles'>\n<li>Article 15 — Accuracy, Robustness, Cybersecurity</li>\n<li>Article 13 — Risk Management</li>\n<li>Article 17 — Transparency to Users</li>\n<li>Article 47 — Audit Right</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Relevant MCPs</h2>\n<p style='color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem'>These MCP servers operationalise compliance for this sector and regulation:</p>\n<span class='mcp-tag'>csoai-eu-ai-act</span> <span class='mcp-tag'>csoai-rms</span> <span class='mcp-tag'>csoai-deployer-pack</span> \n\n<h2>Framework Reference</h2>\n<p>See the full <a href='/frameworks/eu-ai-act'>EU AI Act crosswalk</a> for the published clause-by-clause mappings. The signed crosswalk covers four regimes; anything outside them is described, not crosswalked.</p>\n\n<div class='cta'>\n  <h2>Run the free risk classifier</h2>\n  <p style='color:#e6f7ec;margin:.5rem 0'>The free self-serve tool is an EU AI Act risk classifier: describe the system in text and a deterministic decision table returns the Annex III tier and the gaps against a fixed Art 9–15/50 control set. It covers one regulation, it never contacts your system, and it is not a bench run. A GSPC bench run against a frozen bank is arranged directly and is not yet self-serve.</p>\n  <a href='/certify'>Get Measured &rarr;</a>\n  <a href='/asti'>See AI Self-State Index</a>\n  <a href='/frameworks'>All Frameworks</a>\n</div>\n\n<p class='foot'>&copy; 2026 CSOAI LTD &middot; UK Companies House <strong>16939677</strong><br>\nSector crosswalk &middot; CC BY 4.0 &middot; <a href='/methodology'>Methodology</a> &middot; <a href='mailto:nicholas@csoai.org'>Contact</a><br>\n<em>\"The ISO for AI safety.\"</em></p>",
