    "content": "<p class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\">CSOAI</a> · <a href=\"/frameworks\">Frameworks</a> · <a href=\"/frameworks/cra\">CRA</a> · Non-profit & NGO</p> <p style=\"text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600\">Sector Compliance</p> <h1>Non-profit & NGO AI Compliance: CRA</h1> <p class=\"lead\">Non-profit & NGO organisations using AI must comply with CRA. Humanitarian, advocacy and social impact AI. Cyber Resilience Act. Security requirements for products with digital elements.. CSOAI publishes a signed crosswalk and signed measurement records with public verify URLs. The published crosswalk covers four regimes (EU, UK, Illinois SB 315, TC260) at /crosswalk/east-west-v1.json; mappings beyond those four are described rather than crosswalked, and this page says which is which.</p> <h2>Key CRA Requirements for Non-profit & NGO</h2> <div class=\"req-box\"><h4>Article 10 — Security Requirements</h4><p>CSOAI maps this to charter articles. The mapping is indicative and published; the signed, article-level crosswalk runs in the OS.</p></div> <div class=\"req-box\"><h4>Article 13 — Vulnerability Handling</h4><p>CSOAI maps this to charter articles. The mapping is indicative and published; the signed, article-level crosswalk runs in the OS.</p></div> <div class=\"req-box\"><h4>Article 14 — Security Updates</h4><p>CSOAI maps this to charter articles. The mapping is indicative and published; the signed, article-level crosswalk runs in the OS.</p></div> <h2>CSOAI Compliance Coverage</h2> <div class=\"req-box\"> <h4>Crosswalk mapping — indicative, not a determination</h4> <p>CSOAI maps CRA requirements to a published control set. The mapping is indicative; we enforce nothing — only a regulator can. Every mapping is published as a crosswalk. The measurement behind it is re-runnable from the published harness — we are not claiming a live consensus process.</p> </div> <div class=\"req-box\"> <h4>Signed Attestations</h4> <p>Every measurement run is signed, and its inputs are published, so anyone can recompute the result rather than trust it. Public verify URL: https://councilof.ai/gspc-verify</p> </div> <div class=\"req-box\"> <h4>The Measured Board</h4> <p>Published on the signed board: every axis with its item count and confidence interval where quotable (usable n ≥ 30) — the slot count and the measured count are published together on the live board (GET /api/gspc, totals.public_count) and are deliberately not frozen into this page. UNMEASURED cells are shown empty, never invented. Verify any card free at councilof.ai/gspc-verify.</p> </div> <h2>Get Measured</h2> <p>Run a CSOAI measurement against the EU AI Act — verification free forever.</p> <a href=\"/gspc-verify\" class=\"cta\">Run the free measurement →</a> <p class=\"foot\">© 2026 CSOAI LTD (UK 16939677) · <a href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a> · <a href=\"/asti\">ASSTI Benchmark</a></p>",
