    "css": " .legacy-content :root{--ink:#0f172a;--muted:#5a5e66;--gold:#c9a84c;--card:#f7f8fa;--border:#e6e8ec;--brand:#0a8a3f} .legacy-content body{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;max-width:880px;margin:2.5rem auto;padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.65} .legacy-content h1{margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:2.3rem;letter-spacing:-.02em} .legacy-content h2{margin-top:2.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding-bottom:.4rem;font-size:1.4rem} .legacy-content a{color:var(--brand);text-decoration:none} .legacy-content a:hover{text-decoration:underline} .legacy-content .lead{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.1rem;max-width:720px;margin-top:.75rem} .legacy-content .req-box{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.55rem;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;margin:1rem 0} .legacy-content .req-box h4{margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:1rem} .legacy-content .req-box p{margin:0;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)} .legacy-content .cta{display:inline-block;background:var(--brand);color:white;padding:.85rem 1.5rem;border-radius:.5rem;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;margin-top:.5rem} .legacy-content .foot{margin-top:3rem;color:#888;font-size:.85rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:1.5rem} .legacy-content .breadcrumb{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem} .legacy-content .breadcrumb a{color:var(--muted)} ",
    "content": "<p class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\">CSOAI</a> · <a href=\"/frameworks\">Frameworks</a> · <a href=\"/frameworks/nis2\">NIS2</a> · Non-profit & NGO</p> <p style=\"text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600\">Sector Compliance</p> <h1>Non-profit & NGO AI Compliance: NIS2</h1> <p class=\"lead\">Non-profit & NGO organisations using AI must comply with NIS2. Humanitarian, advocacy and social impact AI. Network and Information Security Directive. Expands scope to important entities across all sectors.. CSOAI publishes a signed crosswalk and signed measurement records with public verify URLs for NIS2. The published crosswalk covers four regimes (EU, UK, Illinois SB 315, TC260) at /crosswalk/east-west-v1.json; mappings beyond those four are described rather than crosswalked.</p> <h2>Key NIS2 Requirements for Non-profit & NGO</h2> <div class=\"req-box\"><h4>Article 21 — Cybersecurity Risk Management</h4><p>CSOAI maps this to charter articles. The mapping is indicative and published; the signed, article-level crosswalk runs in the OS.</p></div> <div class=\"req-box\"><h4>Article 23 — Incident Reporting</h4><p>CSOAI maps this to charter articles. The mapping is indicative and published; the signed, article-level crosswalk runs in the OS.</p></div> <h2>CSOAI Compliance Coverage</h2> <div class=\"req-box\"> <h4>Crosswalk mapping — indicative, not a determination</h4> <p>CSOAI maps NIS2 requirements to a published control set. The mapping is indicative; we enforce nothing — only a regulator can. Every mapping is published as a crosswalk. The measurement behind it is re-runnable from the published harness — we are not claiming a live consensus process.</p> </div> <div class=\"req-box\"> <h4>Signed Attestations</h4> <p>Every measurement run is signed, and its inputs are published, so anyone can recompute the result rather than trust it. Public verify URL: https://councilof.ai/gspc-verify</p> </div> <div class=\"req-box\"> <h4>The Measured Board</h4> <p>Published on the signed board: every axis with its item count and confidence interval where quotable (usable n ≥ 30) — the slot count and the measured count are published together on the live board (GET /api/gspc, totals.public_count) and are deliberately not frozen into this page. UNMEASURED cells are shown empty, never invented. Verify any card free at councilof.ai/gspc-verify.</p> </div> <h2>Get Measured</h2> <p>Run a CSOAI measurement against the EU AI Act — verification free forever.</p> <a href=\"/gspc-verify\" class=\"cta\">Run the free measurement →</a> <p class=\"foot\">© 2026 CSOAI LTD (UK 16939677) · <a href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a> · <a href=\"/asti\">ASSTI Benchmark</a></p>",
