    "content": "<div style='display:flex;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem'><span class='tag'>European Union</span> <span class='tag'>2022</span></div>\n<h1>Retail / E-commerce AI Compliance: NIS2</h1>\n<p class='lead'>Large e-commerce platforms, digital marketplaces, and retailers operating critical supply-chain infrastructure may qualify as important entities under NIS2. Their AI systems — from demand forecasting to logistics optimisation — must satisfy enhanced cybersecurity requirements.</p>\n\n<div class='meta-bar'>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>Sector:</strong> Retail / E-commerce</span>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>Regulation:</strong> NIS2</span>\n  <span class='tag'><strong>CSOAI Articles:</strong> 4 mapped</span>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Key Compliance Requirements</h2>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Entity classification for large retailers</h3><p>Large e-commerce platforms and digital marketplaces may be designated as important entities under NIS2 Annex II based on their scale and societal role.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Cybersecurity risk management for retail AI</h3><p>Article 21 requires proportionate measures for AI systems handling customer data, payment information, and supply-chain operations.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Supply-chain security for retail AI vendors</h3><p>Retailers must assess cybersecurity practices of AI personalisation, demand-forecasting, and logistics-optimisation vendors.</p></div>\n<div class='requirement-box'><h3>Incident reporting for customer-data breaches</h3><p>Significant cyber incidents affecting customer personal or payment data must be reported within 24 hours to national CSIRTs.</p></div>\n\n<h2>CSOAI Charter Articles</h2>\n<ul class='articles'>\n<li>Article 22 — Right to Safety</li>\n<li>Article 26 — Adversarial Resilience</li>\n<li>Article 39 — Incident Response</li>\n<li>Article 47 — Audit Right</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Relevant MCPs</h2>\n<p style='color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem'>These MCP servers operationalise compliance for this sector and regulation:</p>\n<span class='mcp-tag'>nis2-cybersecurity-assessor-mcp</span> <span class='mcp-tag'>nis2-article-checker-mcp</span> <span class='mcp-tag'>csoai-cra</span> \n\n<h2>Framework Reference</h2>\n<p>See the full <a href='/frameworks/nis2'>NIS2 crosswalk</a> for the published clause-by-clause mappings. The signed crosswalk covers four regimes; anything outside them is described, not crosswalked.</p>\n\n<div class='cta'>\n  <h2>Run the free risk classifier</h2>\n  <p style='color:#e6f7ec;margin:.5rem 0'>The free self-serve tool is an EU AI Act risk classifier: describe the system in text and a deterministic decision table returns the Annex III tier and the gaps against a fixed Art 9–15/50 control set. It covers one regulation, it never contacts your system, and it is not a bench run. A GSPC bench run against a frozen bank is arranged directly and is not yet self-serve.</p>\n  <a href='/certify'>Get Measured &rarr;</a>\n  <a href='/asti'>See AI Self-State Index</a>\n  <a href='/frameworks'>All Frameworks</a>\n</div>\n\n<p class='foot'>&copy; 2026 CSOAI LTD &middot; UK Companies House <strong>16939677</strong><br>\nSector crosswalk &middot; CC BY 4.0 &middot; <a href='/methodology'>Methodology</a> &middot; <a href='mailto:nicholas@csoai.org'>Contact</a><br>\n<em>\"The ISO for AI safety.\"</em></p>",
